# Loge: egglog smoke test

```elixir
root = Path.expand("..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:loge, path: Path.join(root, "loge"), override: true},
  {:loge_egglog, path: Path.join(root, "loge_egglog")},
  {:kino_loge, path: Path.join(root, "kino_loge")}
])
```

## Running

Expected: **completed**, the extracted term `(Add (Num 2) (Num 3))` or `(Add (Num 3) (Num 2))`.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(datatype Math (Num i64) (Add Math Math) (Mul Math Math))\n(rewrite (Add a b) (Add b a))\n(rewrite (Mul a (Num 1)) a)\n\n(let e (Add (Mul (Num 2) (Num 1)) (Num 3)))\n(run 5)\n(check (= e (Add (Num 3) (Num 2))))\n(extract e)\n",
  graph: false
)
```

With **Show the e-graph** on, the Result tab also draws the e-graph: each e-class a box of its e-nodes.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(datatype Math (Num i64) (Add Math Math) (Mul Math Math))\n(rewrite (Add a b) (Add b a))\n(rewrite (Mul a (Num 1)) a)\n\n(let e (Add (Mul (Num 2) (Num 1)) (Num 3)))\n(run 5)\n",
  graph: true
)
```

A failed check: expected **check failed**, egglog's message in the Output tab.

<!-- livebook:{"attrs":"","chunks":null,"kind":"Elixir.KinoLoge.Cell","livebook_object":"smart_cell"} -->

```elixir
Loge.run!(
  Loge.Egglog.Engines.Egglog,
  "(datatype Math (Num i64) (Add Math Math) (Mul Math Math))\n(rewrite (Add a b) (Add b a))\n(rewrite (Mul a (Num 1)) a)\n\n(let e (Add (Mul (Num 2) (Num 1)) (Num 3)))\n(run 5)\n(check (= e (Num 5)))\n",
  graph: false
)
```

This run grows without bound. Expected: it runs until stopped; stopping the evaluation ends it.

